## 3. Live telemetry: does Serbian actually reach Nova, and what happens

Queried Supabase (project inmkhvwdcuyhnxkgfvsb) `oasis_events` via the
Supabase REST/RPC path available to this session — read-only, no writes.
`vtid.live.session.start` carries `lang`; the paired
`vtid.live.session.stop` does not, so the two are joined by `session_id`.

Conceptual query (executed via the Supabase MCP/REST query interface, not
raw psql — no direct Postgres port is reachable from this session):

  WITH starts AS (
    SELECT metadata->>'session_id' AS session_id,
           metadata->>'lang'       AS lang,
           created_at              AS started_at
    FROM oasis_events
    WHERE topic = 'vtid.live.session.start'
      AND metadata->>'lang' = 'sr'
      AND created_at > now() - interval '7 days'
  ),
  stops AS (
    SELECT metadata->>'session_id'      AS session_id,
           metadata->>'turn_count'      AS turn_count,
           metadata->>'audio_out_chunks' AS audio_out_chunks,
           metadata->>'reason'          AS reason,
           metadata->>'code'            AS code,
           metadata->>'diagnostic'      AS diagnostic
    FROM oasis_events
    WHERE topic = 'vtid.live.session.stop'
  )
  SELECT s.session_id, s.started_at, t.turn_count, t.audio_out_chunks,
         t.reason, t.code, t.diagnostic
  FROM starts s JOIN stops t USING (session_id)
  ORDER BY s.started_at DESC;

Result: 20 rows. See outputs/serbian-telemetry-notes.md for the aggregate
breakdown and interpretation (raw rows omitted — they carry real
`session_id`s and are not committed verbatim).

